==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|irrégularité|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{term|irregularitas|lang=la}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|irregularities}}

# {{context|countable|lang=en}} An instance of being [[irregular]].
# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} The state or condition of being irregular, or the extent to which something is irregular.
# {{context|countable|lang=en}} An [[object]] or [[event]] that is not [[regular]] or [[ordinary]].
#: ''an '''irregularity''' of surface''
# {{context|countable|lang=en}} A [[violation]] of rules.
#: ''An investigation of the '''irregularities''' in the company's accounts uncovered a large-scale fraud.''
# {{context|euphemism}} Diarrhea. 

====Related terms====
* {{l/en|irregular}}

